expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:strictly-stronger}
For closure operators $c,d$ on $L$, write $c \prec d$ (``$d$ is strictly stronger than $c$'') if
$c\le d$ and there exists an $x\in L$ such that $d(x)\neq c(x)$.

