expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:sau-first-boundary-support}
A first boundary for a hidden node \(h\in\Hid_\ast(\mathfrak T)\) is a boundary node \(b\in\operatorname{Bd}(\mathfrak T)\cap\operatorname{Anc}(v_\ast)\) such that \(h\leadsto b\) and no lower-visible node strictly between \(h\) and \(b\) on the selected dependency path is already fed by \(h\).  Because \(D\) is finite and \(v_\ast\) is lower-visible in an accepted trace, at least one such first boundary exists for every essential hidden node.

The hidden support of \(b\), written \(H_b\), is the finite promoted subtrace consisting of all hidden promoted ancestors of \(b\) that feed \(b\) without passing through an earlier lower-visible audit-boundary node.  The boundary expression of \(H_b\), written \(C_b(H_b)\), is the object carried by \(b\) together with the audited rule data that turns \(H_b\) into \(o(b)\).

